species.cow.desc=Calm, patient and fond of a good long chew. Cows wander open meadows and remember every kind face.
species.cow.rare=Some say a cow with a coat as dark as cocoa roams the far meadows.
species.chicken.desc=Busy, chatty and always certain there is a seed somewhere nearby. Chickens like company and a dusty corner.
species.chicken.rare=Now and then a hen with shining golden feathers wanders in from the wild.
species.pig.desc=Clever noses and big appetites. Pigs love a cool wallow and will happily dig for treasure.
species.pig.rare=A spotted pig, they say, can sniff out a truffle from across a field.
species.sheep.desc=Soft, gentle and happiest in a little flock. Sheep graze all day and spring about when they are pleased.
species.sheep.rare=A sheep with wool as black as night has been seen among the hills.
species.frog.desc=Round, damp and wonderfully content. Frogs keep to still water and sing to each other at dusk.
species.frog.rare=Old ponds sometimes hide a frog of a most unusual colour.

